  "id": "Compound::DB00184 - Gene::1135",
  "verbalization": "Nicotine is implicated in the regulation of Acetylcholine-activated Cation-selective Channel Activity through its interaction with multiple nicotinic receptor subunits, namely Chrna5, Chrna6, and Chrna3. These subunits participate in the same biological process, which is central to the function of nicotinic acetylcholine receptors. The evidence suggests that Nicotine binds to these receptors, triggering a cascade of cellular responses that ultimately involve Chrna2. The shared participation of these receptors in the same pathway implies a potential mechanism by which Nicotine influences the expression or activity of Chrna2, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of nicotinic receptors in modulating ion channel activity, underscoring the importance of Chrna2 in the broader context of nicotinic signaling.",
